WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
Writer/Instructor and Script Consultant Shannan&nbsp;
E. Johnson (The Professional Pen): One of my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.120
favorite examples is using Scandal. We open&nbsp;
up Scandal hearing from two other people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.120
talk about Olivia Pope [played by Kerry&nbsp;
Washington], one of them is the trusted source.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.040
Film Courage: How does a writer introduce&nbsp;
a protagonist in a way that makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.560
the viewer or reader want&nbsp;
to follow that character?

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:27.120
Shannan: Good question. I actually did an entire&nbsp;
workshop on How Do I and I call them How The F?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:34.080
All of my workshops are in the What The F workshop&nbsp;
series. This particular workshop was How The F Do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:41.520
I Introduce My Protagonist and there are a million&nbsp;
ways to do it but what we're looking for is what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.720
information are you going to give me about them&nbsp;
in their normal life that makes me like them or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:52.160
relate to them? I don't have to do both. It's 2021&nbsp;
so I don't have to like the character. They can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:58.560
totally unlikable but something about them has&nbsp;
to be able to relate to in order to care enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:06.080
and invest in them on this journey. So I use the&nbsp;
word social proof and basically what that means is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.280
prove to me (going back to the evidence), prove&nbsp;
to me who they are on the page whether that means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:18.080
we're receiving information from someone else or&nbsp;
we're watching them do the thing because just like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.440
regular human beings you can only take what&nbsp;
they say about themselves with a grain of salt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.840
so I can sit here and go I'm an expert I'm an&nbsp;
expert I'm an expert but unless you actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:35.440
hear me giving my expertise on something or you&nbsp;
hear from someone else who you trust who says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:42.560
Shannan is an expert then you're probably gonna&nbsp;
say I'm not one so on the page you have to then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.600
show us that your characters are whoever&nbsp;
it is you want us to believe that they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:54.800
so one of my favorite examples is using Scandal&nbsp;
we open up Scandal hearing from two other people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:01.920
talk about Olivia Pope one of them is the trusted&nbsp;
source the other one is the fish out of water who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.960
already has some kind of admiration for Olivia&nbsp;
Pope so as we're hearing them talk about Olivia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:14.480
they're putting her on this pedestal and now we&nbsp;
are therefore intrigued to go well who's this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:20.240
Olivia I want to know her she seems cool and&nbsp;
then in the next scene Olivia now has to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.600
up to the thing that we just heard so now you&nbsp;
have to show us in action they could have gone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.600
to the next scene and Olivia was just sitting&nbsp;
there having a meeting talking on the phone to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:35.760
herself but instead they put her in a situation&nbsp;
to show her social proof in doing her job and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.280
so hearing from those other people first and then&nbsp;
seeing her actually do the thing is what made us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.200
want to journey with Olivia Pope so the same is&nbsp;
true for your characters there is no particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:54.400
kind of formula but what I will say is you got&nbsp;
about five to seven minutes to get me engaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.160
with your protagonist some stories won't&nbsp;
start with the protagonist which is fine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.880
but that means if it didn't start with the&nbsp;
protagonist and then we meet them you have less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.680
time to get me to like or relate to them because&nbsp;
I'm already x amount of minutes into your film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.840
so for example I'm teaching from armageddon now we&nbsp;
don't meet harry stamper I think a snapper until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.600
like page 10 which means we're we've been here&nbsp;
for 10 minutes already because we got our exciting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.360
incident on page two so that means the urgency&nbsp;
is already there they're already making up a plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:34.720
by the time we meet harry I only get like three&nbsp;
pages to really understand who he is and jump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.440
into action with him to decide to invest in him&nbsp;
so now you have even less time because I'm already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:48.000
10 minutes into it but either way whatever it is I&nbsp;
see them doing first so you can't be generic about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:53.200
that like oftentimes I will read a screenplay and&nbsp;
it's just oh such and such woman who's beautiful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.480
is cooking breakfast and it just seems like she's&nbsp;
cooking breakfast because she needs busy work in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:04.960
the kitchen not because cooking breakfast teaches&nbsp;
us anything about her is she cooking breakfast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.760
because she's a stay-at-home mom and she's in her&nbsp;
pajamas and she has to get up early even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.920
she's going to be at home but because she's got&nbsp;
to get husband out she's got to get kids out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.280
she's getting it done or is she career woman who's&nbsp;
cooking breakfast so she doesn't really have much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.720
time because she's on the phone at the same time&nbsp;
she's just trying to get something in and it's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:29.040
smoothie and she's running out or is this Saturday&nbsp;
the only day that she gets to relax and she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.920
making brunch because her girlfriends are coming&nbsp;
over like what does it mean and what am I learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:39.440
about this person as their cooking eggs because if&nbsp;
not they could be doing something else what I mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:43.920
so every single piece of information that&nbsp;
I get in those first five to seven minutes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.000
are going to help me know who they are and&nbsp;
that's prime real estate and a lot of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:54.640
pass through that prime real estate by doing the&nbsp;
uncle such and such thing talking about all this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.680
other stuff that does not matter meanwhile all&nbsp;
I got about my protagonist was beautiful and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:06.720
cooking eggs why am I invested in her what how is&nbsp;
that interesting why would any actor who reads it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:12.560
say I gotta play her so you're trying to give&nbsp;
me some information that's going to give me a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.640
reason to invest in the rest of their journey&nbsp;
and you only get a very short amount of time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:22.800
okay so if something doesn't happen within&nbsp;
a five to seven minute minute mark to show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:30.480
me why I should care about the scene so then if&nbsp;
we have this woman cooking these eggs and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:37.440
maybe there's a knock at the door and it's&nbsp;
some door-to-door salesman so we think and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:43.280
it turns out it's really a private investigator&nbsp;
and they're saying I have something for you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.640
and her life is about to change in that moment and&nbsp;
she finds out that her life and what she thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:53.760
it was wasn't really that but we don't know in&nbsp;
that moment so everything seems calm and wonderful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:58.320
and she's beautiful and she has this nice&nbsp;
kitchen but then the knock at the door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:03.360
is going to be what's going to upset the apple&nbsp;
cart yes but I want to make sure that we separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:10.800
the two things that that upset of the apple cart&nbsp;
can happen 15 pages in it can happen 17 pages in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:18.320
everything that I'm getting up until that upset is&nbsp;
what's making me invest in her why do I care that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.000
her life is going to change if I haven't learned&nbsp;
anything about her life other than the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:28.000
she cooks eggs what information are you going to&nbsp;
give me does she have a child that she's caring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:32.880
for that they have a really great relationship&nbsp;
with does she have a husband that she has a bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.440
relationship with and she's just today's the day&nbsp;
they're supposed to go to therapy and she just&nbsp;&nbsp;

